  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">How we started</p>
    <h2 class="mt-2 text-3xl sm:text-4xl">Built around a love of Roman cooking</h2>
    <div class="prose-roma mt-5 space-y-4">
      <p>
        Via Roma started with a simple idea: a restaurant should feel like an
        extension of someone's home. Not a special-occasion-only kind of
        place, but somewhere you'd bring your family on a Tuesday and still
        feel like the evening mattered.
      </p>
      <p>
        The menu leans on the cooking of Rome — the kind built on a handful
        of good ingredients, handled carefully. Cacio e pepe with just
        pecorino, pepper, and pasta water. A ragù that's had all afternoon.
        Bread and olive oil that don't need anything else.
      </p>
      <p>
        We keep the kitchen close to the dining room, the pasta handmade, and
        the hospitality unhurried. That's the whole approach.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

